= Tubby Cut =
#icon: SOP/HDA_Icon.png

"""Performs a boolean operation with a cylinderical shape in a selection of points."""


== Overview ==


Tubby Cut is a utility that performs cylindrical boolean operations for hard surface modeling.

It was created to speed up the process of performing boolean operations with clean topology.

It results in a clean topology that includes quads and outputs groups to be used.

@parameters


== General Settings ==


Operation:
    #id: operation

    Defines the boolean operation that is going to be performed.

Points Group:
    #id: points_group

    The group name for the selection of points. This is the selection of points the operation is going to be performed to.
    

== Operator Settings ==


Shape:
    #id: shape

    Choose either a Tube or a Sphere shape as the boolean operator.

Radius:
    #id: radius

    The radius of the shape that acts as the boolean operator.

Height:
    #id: height

    The height of the shape that acts as the boolean operator. This is only available for the Tube shape.

Cap:
    #id: cap

    Toggles the cap fill for the shape that acts as the boolean operator.
    
Fill:
    #id: fill

    Choose between a Quads or a Triangles fill for the cap of the shape.

Quads Offset:
    #id: quads_offset

    Offset the quads pattern for the cap fill of the shape. This is only available when Fill is set to Quads.


== Output Groups ==

    
=== Primitives Group ===
   

Operator Wall:
    #id: op_wall

    This is the group for the side primitives of the shape that acts as the boolean operator.

Operator Cap:
    #id: op_cap

    This is the group for the cap fill primitives of the shape that acts as the boolean operator.

Surface Perimeter:
    #id: surface_perimeter

    This is the group for the side primitives of the geometry the boolean operation is performed to.
    
Surface Rest:
    #id: surface_rest

    This is the group for the rest primitives of the geometry the boolean operation is performed to.

    
=== Edges Group ===


Operator Edges:
    #id: op_edges

    This is the group for the cap fill edges of the shape that acts as the boolean operator.

Surface Edges:
    #id: surface_edges

    This is the group for the intersecting edges of the shape that acts as the boolean operator and the geometry that is performed to.

   
@related

